          "evidence_state": "explicit_text",
          "pointer_state": "resolved",
          "source_value": "Arbitrary randomized adaptive algorithms are allowed, but both points in a batch must be fixed before its seed is drawn. Queries, stopping, and postprocessing may be arbitrary measurable functions; outputs may be unqueried, randomly selected historical points, or admissible averages. No span or zero-respecting restriction is imposed. Queries are sequential, and each response in a batch is charged. Internal arithmetic, linear algebra, and storage are free; internal work, memory, and communication are not budgeted.",
